ning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"A to-infinitive cannot follow for in this action-complement pattern.","B":"A base verb is not the standard complement after for here.","C":"A past form is not the -ing clause required after for.","D":"After preposition **for**, use **measuring** to name the action being apologised for."}}},{"id":"6b3906b2-c3fd-5f9d-aaf5-96572aea79f4","topicSlug":"reporting-verb-patterns","level":"C1","prompt":"“She promised ____ the travel leaflet before lunch.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"to translate"},{"id":"B","text":"translating"},{"id":"C","text":"translate"},{"id":"D","text":"translated"}],"answerId":"A","hint":"The reporting verb **promise** takes a **to-infinitive** for the promised action.","explanation":"**Promise to translate** reports her commitment to perform the action.","keywords":["promise-infinitive"],"skill":"promise-infinitive","contextKey":"reporting-verb-patterns-4","fingerprint":"cb6f7367f96678e872159477d22feb856431b9ab14bb84690370282e3a38f7eb","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-reporting-patterns"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The reporting verb **promise** takes a **to-infinitive** for the promised action.","**Promise to translate** reports her commitment to perform the action.","Choose **to translate**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"**Promise to translate** reports her commitment to perform the action.","B":"Promise does not normally take this bare -ing complement for a commitment.","C":"Promise needs to before the infinitive in this pattern.","D":"A past form cannot serve as the infinitive complement."}}},{"id":"407c35d1-a6e9-59fe-abc6-b5c92707e34a","topicSlug":"reporting-verb-patterns","level":"C1","prompt":"“He reminded us ____ the travel leaflet before leaving.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"to translate"},{"id":"B",